   "_dt": 1793030114.0,
   "ageDays": 0.09,
   "summary": "Around this time, a familiar question returns to the public space: “Are we producing too many lawyers?” It is a fair question. Too many lawyers for which roles, in which locations, and measured against what demand? Over two decades ago, as I prepared to enter university, my brother-in-law, Kofi Agamah, connected me with Mr Egyir Croffet at the University of Ghana’s Counselling and Placement Centre to help me decide what to study.",
   "summary_zh": "每到这个时候，一个熟悉的问题便会重新出现在公共讨论中：“我们培养的律师是否太多了？”这是一个合理的问题。究竟是哪些岗位需要太多律师，在哪些地区需要，又该以什么需求为衡量标准？二十多年前，在我准备进入大学时，姐夫科菲·阿加马联系了加纳大学咨询与就业中心的埃吉尔·克罗夫特先生，帮助我决定学习什么专业。",
   "summarySource": "index",
   "body": "Seeing people you once taught put on their wigs and gowns brings a special satisfaction. You remember their questions, their struggles, and their determination. Their achievement becomes part of your reward for teaching. Around this time, a familiar question returns to the public space: “Are we producing too many lawyers?” It is a fair question. What is curious is how readily we offer answers without establishing the context or examining the data. Too many lawyers for which roles, in which locations, and measured against what demand? Over two decades ago, as I prepared to enter university, my brother-in-law, Kofi Agamah, connected me with Mr Egyir Croffet at the University of Ghana’s Counselling and Placement Centre to help me decide what to study. One of the tools Mr Croffet and his colleague, Mr Wiafe, used during that process was the United States’ Occupational Outlook Handbook. Publi",
