   "title": "919749 state police 24 states approve constitutional amendment presidential panel",
   "url": "https://www.premiumtimesng.com/news/top-news/919749-state-police-24-states-approve-constitutional-amendment-presidential-panel.html",
   "domain": "premiumtimesng.com",
   "source": "Premium Times（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:33:49 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792794829.0,
   "ageDays": 2.81,
   "summary": "The Presidential Working Group on the National Policing Bill says 24 State Houses of Assembly have approved the Constitution (Sixth Alteration) Bill, 2026, providing for a dual policing system. The approval meets the constitutional threshold of two-thirds of the 36 states required for the amendment to proceed. The working group commended the state Houses of Assembly for their action and acknowledged the National Assembly for passing the amendment in both chambers.",
   "summary_zh": "国家警务法案总统工作组表示，24个州议会已批准《2026年宪法（第六次修订）法案》，其中规定实行双重警务制度。此次批准达到了修宪所需的门槛，即36个州中三分之二以上州议会的同意，使修宪得以推进。工作组赞扬各州议会采取的行动，并承认国民议会在两院均通过了该修正案。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Presidential Working Group on the National Policing Bill says 24 State Houses of Assembly have approved the Constitution (Sixth Alteration) Bill, 2026, providing for a dual policing system. The approval meets the constitutional threshold of two-thirds of the 36 states required for the amendment to proceed. The working group commended the state Houses of Assembly for their action and acknowledged the National Assembly for passing the amendment in both chambers. This is contained in a statement issued by Femi Gbajabiamila, chief of staff to the President and chairman of the group, on Friday in Abuja. Mr Gbajabiamila said the approval provided constitutional backing for the policing framework outlined in the working group’s draft National Policing Bill, 2026. He added that the draft Bills were undergoing legislative drafting review and validation at the Federal Ministry of Justice. The Bills are expected to be returned on or before 30 October, after which the working group will give them final consideration before presenting them to President Bola Tinubu. The working group urged stakeholders to support a smooth transition to a dual policing system aimed at improving public safety",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
